## Best Practices

### 1. Model Selection

Choose the right model for your use case:

| Use Case | Recommended Model | Why |
|----------|------------------|-----|
| Outpainting / Canvas Extension | Flux Fill Pro | Best mask support, high quality fills |
| Banner Resizing (1:1 → 4:1) | Flux Fill Pro | Intelligent content-aware extension |
| Quick General Edits | OpenRouter (default) | Fast, natural language, creative |
| Consistent Edits | InstructPix2Pix | Stable, predictable results |
| Object Removal | Flux Fill Pro | Superior inpainting quality |
| Color/Style Changes | OpenRouter | Great for global adjustments |

### 2. Prompt Engineering

Write clear, specific instructions:

```typescript
// ❌ Bad: Vague
{ prompt: "make it better" }

// ✅ Good: Specific
{ prompt: "Increase brightness by 20%, add warm sunset tones, enhance contrast" }

// ❌ Bad: Ambiguous
{ prompt: "change background" }

// ✅ Good: Descriptive
{ prompt: "Replace background with modern office interior, natural lighting, blurred bokeh effect" }
```

### 3. Mask Creation Best Practices

For Flux Fill Pro inpainting/outpainting:

```typescript
// Create mask programmatically
function createOutpaintMask(originalWidth, originalHeight, newWidth, newHeight) {
  const canvas = document.createElement('canvas');
  canvas.width = newWidth;
  canvas.height = newHeight;
  const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');

  // Fill entire canvas with white (areas to fill)
  ctx.fillStyle = 'white';
  ctx.fillRect(0, 0, newWidth, newHeight);

  // Draw black rectangle for original image area (preserve)
  ctx.fillStyle = 'black';
  ctx.fillRect(
    (newWidth - originalWidth) / 2,
    (newHeight - originalHeight) / 2,
    originalWidth,
    originalHeight
  );

  return canvas.toDataURL();
}

// Example: Extend 400x400 square to 1584x396 banner
const mask = createOutpaintMask(400, 400, 1584, 396);
```

**Mask Guidelines:**
- White = Edit/fill this area
- Black = Keep original content
- Use grayscale for soft transitions
- Match mask dimensions to target output

### 4. Image Format Optimization

Prepare images for best results:

```typescript
// Convert to data URI for reliability
async function imageUrlToDataUri(url) {
  const response = await fetch(url);
  const blob = await response.blob();

  return new Promise((resolve) => {
    const reader = new FileReader();
    reader.onloadend = () => resolve(reader.result);
    reader.readAsDataURL(blob);
  });
}

// Use in request
const imageDataUri = await imageUrlToDataUri(imageUrl);
const response = await fetch('/api/ai/image/edit', {
  method: 'POST',
  body: JSON.stringify({
    image: imageDataUri,
    prompt: 'Make professional'
  })
});
```

### 5. Handling Temporary URLs

Provider URLs expire after ~24 hours. Always download and store:

```typescript
async function editAndStore(image, prompt) {
  // 1. Edit image
  const editResponse = await fetch('/api/ai/image/edit', {
    method: 'POST',
    body: JSON.stringify({ image, prompt })
  });

  const { url: tempUrl } = await editResponse.json();

  // 2. Download immediately
  const imageBlob = await fetch(tempUrl).then(r => r.blob());

  // 3. Upload to your storage (Supabase, S3, etc.)
  const permanentUrl = await uploadToStorage(imageBlob);

  // 4. Save permanent URL to database
  await saveToDatabase({ editedImageUrl: permanentUrl });

  return permanentUrl;
}
```

### 6. Provider Selection Strategy

```typescript
// Use Flux Fill Pro for mask-based edits
if (hasMask) {
  request.model = 'black-forest-labs/flux-fill-pro';
}

// Use OpenRouter for quick iterations
else if (needFastPreview) {
  request.provider = 'openrouter';
}

// Use Replicate for consistent results
else if (needReliability) {
  request.provider = 'replicate';
}

// Default: Let endpoint decide (OpenRouter → Replicate fallback)
```

