## Security Considerations

### API Key Storage

- ✅ API keys stored server-side in database (encrypted)
- ✅ Keys never sent from client or included in responses
- ✅ Automatic fallback to environment variables
- ❌ Never log full API keys (use `!!apiKey` for boolean checks)

### Input Validation

**Server-Side Validation:**
- Request payload structure validated
- Image format automatically normalized (data URI conversion)
- Provider parameter validated against allowed values

**Not Validated:**
- Image content (no NSFW filtering on backend)
- Prompt content (handled by AI providers)
- Mask format (validated by Replicate)

**Safety Considerations:**
- Flux Fill Pro: `safety_tolerance: 5` (balanced setting)
- InstructPix2Pix: No built-in safety checker
- OpenRouter: Model-dependent safety features

### Row-Level Security

User API keys are protected with RLS policies:

```sql
CREATE POLICY "Users can only access their own API keys"
ON user_api_keys
FOR ALL
USING (auth.uid() = user_id);
```

### Cost Control

- Rate limiting prevents abuse (30 req/min)
- Per-user API keys enable billing isolation
- Monitor provider usage via dashboards
- Consider implementing usage quotas per user tier

