## Monitoring and Debugging

### Datadog Traces

View image editing traces in Datadog APM:

**Trace Queries:**
```
operation_name:llm.image_edit_flux      # Flux Fill Pro edits
operation_name:llm.image_edit           # Other edits
```

**Key Metrics:**
- `llm.model_name` - Which model was used
- `llm.provider` - Provider (openrouter/replicate)
- `llm.input` - Edit instruction
- `llm.output` - Result URL
- `error` - Error details if failed

### Log Tags

Console logs use `[Image Edit]` tag:

```typescript
console.warn('[Image Edit] OpenRouter failed, attempting fallback:', err);
console.error('[Image Edit] Replicate fallback failed:', msg);
```

**Search Pattern:** `[Image Edit]`

### Performance Monitoring

**Expected Latency:**

| Provider | Model | Cold Start | Hot |
|----------|-------|------------|-----|
| Flux Fill Pro | flux-fill-pro | 60-180s | 15-30s |
| OpenRouter | gemini-flash | N/A | 2-8s |
| Replicate | InstructPix2Pix | 60-120s | 20-40s |

**Slow Response Causes:**
- Cold start (model not cached)
- Large images (more processing time)
- Complex prompts (more inference steps)
- High provider load (queue delays)

### Debug Checklist

1. Check provider status:
   - Replicate: https://status.replicate.com
   - OpenRouter: https://status.openrouter.ai

2. Verify API keys:
   ```typescript
   console.log('Replicate key:', !!replicateKey);
   console.log('OpenRouter key:', !!openRouterKey);
   ```

3. Check rate limits:
   ```typescript
   console.log('Rate limit headers:', {
     limit: response.headers.get('X-RateLimit-Limit'),
     remaining: response.headers.get('X-RateLimit-Remaining'),
     reset: response.headers.get('X-RateLimit-Reset')
   });
   ```

4. Review Datadog traces for provider errors

5. Test with simpler inputs:
   - Smaller image
   - Simpler prompt
   - No mask

